                  <meta itemprop='url' content='https://discuss.python.org/u/jeanas'>
                (Jean Abou Samra)
              </span>



              <span class="crawler-post-infos">
                  <time itemprop="datePublished" datetime='2023-01-10T23:38:57Z' class='post-time'>
                    January 10, 2023, 11:38pm
                  </time>
                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2023-01-10T23:38:57Z'>
              <span itemprop="position">8</span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class='post' itemprop="text">
              <aside class="quote group-committers" data-username="ambv" data-post="4" data-topic="22606">
<div class="title">
<div class="quote-controls"></div>
<img alt="" width="24" height="24" src="https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/ambv/48/25884_2.png" class="avatar"> Łukasz Langa:</div>
<blockquote>
<p>However, <strong>please note</strong> that on Discourse we avoid posts to show support / agree with the previous poster. Instead, we use the reactions:</p>
</blockquote>
</aside>
<p>The problem is that there’s no way to express a stronger excitement than just “like” <img src="https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12" title=":slight_smile:" class="emoji" alt=":slight_smile:" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"></p>
<p>Minor note: perhaps the PEP should say what happens to the <code>generation</code> argument of<br>
<a href="https://docs.python.org/3/library/gc.html#gc.collect" rel="noopener nofollow ugc">gc.collect</a>.</p>
