          </div>
          <div id='post_20' itemprop="comment" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="http://schema.org/Comment" class='topic-body crawler-post'>
            <div class='crawler-post-meta'>
              <span class="creator" itemprop="author" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="http://schema.org/Person">
                <a rel='nofollow' href='https://discuss.python.org/u/ashbt'><span itemprop="name">ashbt</span></a>
                  <meta itemprop='url' content='https://discuss.python.org/u/ashbt'>
                (Ash Berlin-Taylor)
              </span>



              <span class="crawler-post-infos">
                  <time itemprop="datePublished" datetime='2023-01-11T10:29:07Z' class='post-time'>
                    January 11, 2023, 10:29am
                  </time>
                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2023-01-11T10:29:07Z'>
              <span itemprop="position">20</span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class='post' itemprop="text">
              <p>Somewhat relatedly, this came up in my feed today about a similar issue in bind <a href="https://dotat.at/@/2023-01-10-qsbr.html" class="inline-onebox" rel="noopener nofollow ugc">Safe memory reclamation for BIND – Tony Finch</a> and it talks about <a href="https://liburcu.org/" rel="noopener nofollow ugc">https://liburcu.org/</a> (which is LGPL’d, so I suspect not of use to Python core.)</p>
            </div>

